  "summary": "Alex Miller has been involved in multiple geophysical and volcanic studies within the United States, and abroad. These projects involved geothermal energy exploration, volcanic hazard assessment, lava flow dynamics and volcanic infrasonic/acoustic signals. His research expeditions have included destinations within Iceland, Ecuador, Guatemala and the American Southwest. Miller's familiarity with differing field environments has promoted a global understanding of geophysical deployment.\n\nAs a graduate from North Carolina State University in Natural Resources with a minor in Geology, Miller's attitude of the earth blends both an environmental sciences mentality with a geophysical one.\n\nSpecialties: Field research/deployment, seismic software instillation, seismic analysis",
